  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 758518,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "'89 Dennou Kyuusei Uranai (Fortune Telling '89) is a unique and quirky fortune-telling game for the Nintendo Entertainment System, released in Japan in December 1988. More than just a game, it was a cultural phenomenon, bundled with an almanac to guide players through its predictions. Based on Eastern-style horoscopes, the game forecasts your destiny for 1989 using your date of birth.\n\nDeveloped by Micronics, the game features an unusual aesthetic, including a memorable UFO cat creature prominently displayed on the box art. Gameplay revolves around inputting your birthdate and receiving personalized fortune readings. A notable and peculiar feature is the \"love test,\" where players can input two dates of birth to assess compatibility. However, attempting a same-sex pairing results in a humorous \"crash\" sequence and a message indicating an \"incorrect input.\" While originally designed for 1989, the game's predictive nature renders it largely a nostalgic artifact, offering a glimpse into the past and the computer's predictions for a bygone year."
    },
